[%cachewrite 1558] Black threatens ...Ne3 next, which would fork my queen on c2
and my rook on f1. The knight on e3 would also be defended by the f4 pawn.
Capturing with Nxd5 removes that threat and eliminates Black's best defensive
piece. After the recapture, Black's kingside is thin. Bh7+ then becomes very
strong. If the bishop leaves d3 for h7, my queen on c2 controls the c2–h7
diagonal, so Black cannot answer with Kxh7. If the king steps to f7 instead,
Rxf4+ comes with gain of time. With the knight gone, Black has nothing to
recapture on f4 with. } 21... cxd5 22. Bh7+ { [%emt 0:01:26] [%think 7042]
